rue,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the nanosecond->date conversion before feeding `created_at` to `git rev-list --before=` (e.g. divide by 1e9 and pass `@<seconds>`, or format as ISO-8601), so the floor commit is computed correctly rather than resolving to origin/main tip.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'take the newest main commit at or before the report: git rev-list -1 --before=\"<created_at>\" origin/main'","src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json:42-44: `created_at` is `type: integer`, 'Creation timestamp in nanoseconds (time.time_ns()).'","src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:540-541: 'created_at is the CREATE-event timestamp (ns)'","git `--before=` parses dates / `@<unix-seconds>`; a bare nanosecond integer (~1.7e18) is read as seconds far in the future, so `rev-list -1 --before` matches the newest commit — the FLOOR is silently wrong."],"finding":"Floor source #2 pipes the ticket's `created_at` directly into `git rev-list -1 --before=\"<created_at>\"`, but `created_at` is a nanosecond integer (time.time_ns()), not a date git can parse; git would misinterpret it as a far-future Unix-seconds value and return the newest commit, silently producing a wrong floor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f10dca03f32f01d90","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach > The reported-against floor, source 2","norm_id":"n89c0f155825824f0","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Report quotes no version, so the agent falls back to created_at; the resulting floor is origin/main tip, and the git log diff range is empty — Step 0 reports 'no change since report' when the whole history is actually in scope."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State the conversion explicitly, e.g.: `git rev-list -1 --before=\"@$(( created_at_ns / 1000000000 ))\" origin/main`, or convert the ns integer to an ISO-8601 UTC string and pass that t